# Higher-rank odd symplectic FF parameters

The conditional reduction bounds the original binary dimension using the
faithful image, the actual full normalizer, and automorphisms of the original
central quotient. The numerical comparison leaves `(2,3)`, `(2,5)`, `(2,7)`,
`(3,3)`, `(4,3)` and `(5,3)`. A coefficient-field involution in an offender
gives the additional half-dimension bound by semilinear descent.

The projective degree estimate, symplectic automorphism rank and conjugate
geometry, and the five small exclusions remain to be proved. The exported
conditional assembly is not the source parameter theorem. PSp₄(3) is retained;
its comparison with PSU₄(2) belongs to the separate carrier-comparison owner.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith B.1.13, printed pp.73–74; Guralnick–Malle,
*Classification of 2F-modules, I*, Proposition 4.5, manuscript pp.12–13,
and *II*, Theorem B/Table 2, manuscript p.4. See `Source.md` for the original
hypotheses and the remaining representation work.
-/
